Subject: Cantor B1 Public Verifying Key Custody Attestation Verification P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 78fa6039-c94e-4dfd-843d-85f55b7ec64a

& [Why]
  + A1 signature correspondence identifies a public key but cannot show that a party can use the associated private key
  + a purpose-bound challenge signature supplies proof-of-possession correspondence while explicit false fields prevent that mathematics from laundering self-issued stale replayed exported or shared-key evidence into live custody authority
  + A2 is dependency-next and can be implemented and falsified provider-free before a trusted live challenge custodian identity or protected key store exists

& [WhyNow]
  + A1 implementation and its immediate bookend are published remote equal and replayed
  + NIST and RFC boundaries provide a concrete semantic separation for a small safe executable successor
